1
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:07,674
MEDICAL VOLUNTEER WOMEN'S AWARDS

2
00:00:11,211 --> 00:00:15,181
I am sorry to keep you all waiting.

3
00:00:15,415 --> 00:00:19,986
I would like to now invite
the main guest of the evening.

4
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,955
SURGERY DEPARTMENT PROFESSORS' WIVES

5
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:23,757
INTERNAL MEDICINE DEPARTMENT
PROFESSORS' WIVES

6
00:00:31,097 --> 00:00:31,965
Who is that?

7
00:00:32,399 --> 00:00:36,770
She is showing off her legs so much.
How shameless!

8
00:00:39,773 --> 00:00:42,275
I'm sorry,
but may I ask who you are?

9
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:44,611
- I'm Daimon, a surgeon.
- A surgeon?

10
00:00:46,513 --> 00:00:51,818
No way. She is certainly
not a surgeon's wife.

11
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:55,288
- May I come through?
- Over here.

12
00:00:57,357 --> 00:01:00,460
I told you to come quietly.

13
00:01:00,527 --> 00:01:02,262
That was the only entrance.

14
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,864
- Wow, is this all free?
- Eat as much you want.

15
00:01:05,131 --> 00:01:07,500
Yes! I can't wait.

16
00:01:07,634 --> 00:01:09,736
KANEO KARASUMARA, OFFICE MANAGER

17
00:01:12,038 --> 00:01:16,109
Madam, I am terribly sorry.
I shall begin right away.

18
00:01:16,543 --> 00:01:20,613
Please excuse me.
Once again, I present to you,

19
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:23,249
the main guest of the evening.

20
00:01:23,483 --> 00:01:26,786
Here's the wife
of Executive Manager Hiruma,

21
00:01:26,953 --> 00:01:30,523
the recipient of the Medical
Volunteer Women's Award.

22
00:01:33,293 --> 00:01:36,129
You are our treasure, Mrs. Hiruma.

23
00:01:36,196 --> 00:01:41,568
- Congratulations.
- Congrats.

24
00:01:42,001 --> 00:01:45,371
What is this?
A gathering of bored old ladies?

25
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:49,709
These are the professors' wives at
Teito Medical University Hospital,

26
00:01:50,009 --> 00:01:51,678
a.k.a. the Shirobara Club.

27
00:01:52,545 --> 00:01:54,914
The power relationship
between the professors

28
00:01:54,981 --> 00:01:58,351
and that of their wives are identical.

29
00:01:58,551 --> 00:02:02,655
It seems glamorous,
but behind the scenes,

30
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:06,092
there is an ugly power struggle
among them too.

31
00:02:06,493 --> 00:02:09,195
She is the president
of the Shirobara Club.

32
00:02:09,562 --> 00:02:13,700
She's basically
the director of all the women.

33
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,169
And why are you here, Akira?

34
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:18,104
Why, to get business, of course.

35
00:02:18,571 --> 00:02:20,907
Someone gets fired,
and we'll get a job.

36
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:23,977
Step-by-step effort like this

37
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:27,847
- will turn into big money.
- Bye.

38
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:33,653
Hello. This is a melon.
Please enjoy.

39
00:02:33,853 --> 00:02:35,455
Here you are.

40
00:02:35,855 --> 00:02:40,994
Now I would like to
have Mrs. Hiruma speak for us.

41
00:02:41,294 --> 00:02:42,729
Mrs. Hiruma, please.

42
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:49,102
I am very grateful that
such a wonderful party like this

43
00:02:49,302 --> 00:02:51,204
is being held for me.

44
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:53,239
I believe that everything,

45
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:57,010
including this day,
is all thanks to my husband.

46
00:02:57,177 --> 00:03:02,081
Why did I become a doctor's wife?

47
00:03:02,215 --> 00:03:05,318
I'd like to talk about
how I met my husband.

48
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:09,622
- This is going to be long.
- I'm going to the restroom then.

49
00:03:18,665 --> 00:03:19,766
Are you okay?

50
00:03:22,402 --> 00:03:23,703
I think I had too much wine.

51
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:28,808
Excuse me.

52
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:36,349
Without a good wife,
you can't be a good doctor.

53
00:03:37,283 --> 00:03:41,020
Let's continue to
work hard together.

54
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:47,093
Thanks for a wonderful speech.

55
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,728
Please give it up again for her.

56
00:03:54,701 --> 00:03:57,003
Mrs. Kanie.

57
00:03:57,837 --> 00:04:00,940
You didn't participate in
any volunteering this year.

58
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:03,843
Are you still not feeling well?

59
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:08,348
It makes me wonder
why you even got surgery.

60
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:13,353
No, I was able to recover this much
because I had surgery.

61
00:04:13,987 --> 00:04:19,559
I can't say you seem completely
back to normal, though.

62
00:04:20,793 --> 00:04:25,898
The surgeon was...
Dr. Ebina, wasn't it?

63
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:30,003
Anything wrong with my husband?

64
00:04:32,905 --> 00:04:34,274
It's started again.

65
00:04:34,674 --> 00:04:39,379
Wives of surgery and internal
medicine always get in a fight.

66
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,382
It's like a mongoose and a snake.

67
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:46,352
It's like motorcycle gangs
fighting over territory.

68
00:04:51,557 --> 00:04:54,327
What did you just say?

69
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:00,967
I'm scared.

70
00:05:01,067 --> 00:05:04,437
<i>This is a story</i>
<i>about a maverick female doctor.</i>

71
00:05:04,871 --> 00:05:07,407
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities.</i>

72
00:05:07,607 --> 00:05:13,579
<i>The medical world has become a place</i>
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

73
00:05:15,448 --> 00:05:19,752
<i>To save this crisis</i>
<i>in the world of medical care,</i>

74
00:05:20,353 --> 00:05:23,556
<i>a freelance doctor, in other words,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

75
00:05:25,958 --> 00:05:28,194
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

76
00:05:28,594 --> 00:05:32,165
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

77
00:05:32,231 --> 00:05:33,733
You could at least say hello.

78
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,402
Get rid of your attitude.

79
00:05:36,536 --> 00:05:38,438
Forget it. It's a waste of time.

80
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:40,373
Yes, but sir...

81
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:42,642
I said it's okay. Forget about it.

82
00:05:43,376 --> 00:05:44,277
Yes, sir.

83
00:05:44,410 --> 00:05:49,482
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and on-the-job experience</i>

84
00:05:50,383 --> 00:05:52,719
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

85
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:56,289
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

86
00:06:26,919 --> 00:06:28,321
I'm making my rounds.

87
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:32,658
Professor, your wife is here
to see you.

88
00:06:32,792 --> 00:06:33,693
What?

89
00:06:34,927 --> 00:06:38,498
Calm down...What?
You're calm?

90
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:40,767
Okay...

91
00:06:42,769 --> 00:06:44,137
- Ebina.
- Yes.

92
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:45,805
Something urgent came up.

93
00:06:46,973 --> 00:06:49,609
Take care of making the rounds.

94
00:06:49,675 --> 00:06:52,178
- Yes, sir.
- Bye.

95
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:58,151
- He'll be here right away.
- I see.

96
00:07:25,011 --> 00:07:26,245
Something happened?

97
00:07:26,712 --> 00:07:28,881
I have something important.

98
00:07:29,148 --> 00:07:31,584
I see. You can leave.

99
00:07:32,718 --> 00:07:35,221
Can you try to make it quick?

100
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:37,156
I have a lot of work to do.

101
00:07:38,324 --> 00:07:39,392
Mrs. Kanie?

102
00:07:39,859 --> 00:07:42,361
She embarrassed me at the party.

103
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:45,698
People talked
as if the surgeons are not skilled.

104
00:07:48,334 --> 00:07:49,836
Well...

105
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:52,271
What are you doing?

106
00:07:52,338 --> 00:07:56,209
I was in a hurry
and I hit my knee on the way here.

107
00:07:56,275 --> 00:07:58,177
It's not a big deal.

108
00:07:58,744 --> 00:08:03,149
Mrs. Kanie is a professor's wife
and she is very important.

109
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:07,620
Not being able to cure such a person

110
00:08:07,787 --> 00:08:11,357
affects my status
as the president of the wives' club.

111
00:08:13,192 --> 00:08:17,530
I know, Hanako.
But Mrs. Kanie is completely cured.

112
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:19,532
You can't say that she is cured.

113
00:08:19,932 --> 00:08:21,801
The upcoming chairperson election...

114
00:08:22,635 --> 00:08:26,205
is an important step for you
to be promoted to director.

115
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:29,976
We must crush anything
that would concern us.

116
00:08:30,243 --> 00:08:34,480
I understand. Let's talk about this
in detail some other time.

117
00:08:34,714 --> 00:08:37,416
- In detail?
- Yes. In detail.

118
00:08:39,585 --> 00:08:43,389
Where did you stay last night?

119
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:45,858
Yesterday? Last night,

120
00:08:46,225 --> 00:08:49,161
I slept here...right here.

121
00:08:49,228 --> 00:08:52,765
I had to do research for a thesis.

122
00:08:52,832 --> 00:08:55,034
I slept on the couch like this.

123
00:08:57,637 --> 00:08:58,804
A thesis?

124
00:09:02,808 --> 00:09:04,243
I'm coming in, Professor.

125
00:09:08,114 --> 00:09:08,948
Hello.

126
00:09:09,081 --> 00:09:10,550
Help me.

127
00:09:17,623 --> 00:09:22,194
The International Joint Research
sent the data for Crohn's disease.

128
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:25,865
Thank you. Great job.

129
00:09:25,932 --> 00:09:28,067
Thanks for coming, Kondo.

130
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:31,370
Oh, so you're Dr. Kondo?

131
00:09:32,338 --> 00:09:33,205
Yes.

132
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:39,378
I have heard so much
about you from my husband.

133
00:09:39,445 --> 00:09:40,613
She's my wife.

134
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:44,183
You're Prof. Hiruma's wife?
I didn't realize. You're so young.

135
00:09:45,484 --> 00:09:47,987
How old are you?

136
00:09:48,054 --> 00:09:49,522
I'm 38.

137
00:09:50,389 --> 00:09:53,693
Any plans to get married?
Do you have a girlfriend?

138
00:09:54,026 --> 00:09:55,861
Are you the eldest son?

139
00:09:56,162 --> 00:09:59,632
- Yes, I'm the eldest son.
- He's the eldest son, alright?

140
00:10:00,566 --> 00:10:05,471
Kondo, I know you're busy,
so you can leave.

141
00:10:05,538 --> 00:10:07,473
Yes, thank you.

142
00:10:09,642 --> 00:10:10,576
Goodbye.

143
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:20,252
Does Professor Hiruma have kids?

144
00:10:20,886 --> 00:10:23,889
- Yes, he has a daughter.
- I see.

145
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:33,265
A year ago, Mrs. Kanie had surgery
to cut her small bowel with necrosis.

146
00:10:33,699 --> 00:10:36,802
There is about 30cm left.
The surgery was a success.

147
00:10:37,003 --> 00:10:40,006
For the post-operative
short bowel syndrome,

148
00:10:40,239 --> 00:10:42,208
she's continuing
total parenteral nutrition.

149
00:10:42,842 --> 00:10:44,377
I know that.

150
00:10:45,378 --> 00:10:51,250
Aren't there ways of stopping that
to raise her quality of life?

151
00:10:52,718 --> 00:10:55,755
The only option left is
a small bowel transplant.

152
00:10:56,355 --> 00:10:57,356
Transplant?

153
00:10:59,692 --> 00:11:02,561
Guys, aren't there any other ways?

154
00:11:04,764 --> 00:11:05,998
As of now, no.

155
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,035
Yes!

156
00:11:10,636 --> 00:11:12,071
I'll do it.

157
00:11:12,304 --> 00:11:13,873
- The transplant?
- Yes.

158
00:11:16,876 --> 00:11:18,144
No one will do it, right?

159
00:11:20,613 --> 00:11:21,847
We can't do it.

160
00:11:23,582 --> 00:11:25,651
I see.
There aren't any compatible donors.

161
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:26,852
Why ask if you know?

162
00:11:26,986 --> 00:11:28,587
- In that case...
- What?

163
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:30,923
Hurry up and find a donor.

164
00:11:32,725 --> 00:11:35,728
- Who do you think you're talking to?
- Get out of here.

165
00:11:36,295 --> 00:11:38,064
- Ouch!
- It doesn't hurt.

166
00:11:38,130 --> 00:11:39,665
You're being so rough.

167
00:11:43,903 --> 00:11:45,805
I'm terribly sorry about that.

168
00:11:46,305 --> 00:11:49,608
Professor Hiruma, what shall we do?

169
00:11:52,912 --> 00:11:55,481
Hurry up and find a donor.

170
00:11:58,818 --> 00:11:59,752
Yes, sir.

171
00:12:05,925 --> 00:12:09,128
- Where's the deluxe suite?
- I won't be a guide.

172
00:12:09,261 --> 00:12:13,232
We came from the internal medicine
department to pay a visit to Mrs. Kanie.

173
00:12:13,499 --> 00:12:15,668
- Show us the way!
- I won't do that.

174
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:22,541
Torako, what's wrong?
What's the matter?

175
00:12:24,343 --> 00:12:25,578
Torako, what's wrong?

176
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:29,381
Does it hurt?

177
00:12:39,291 --> 00:12:41,527
I knew it. Hey, Vice Commander.

178
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:44,797
- Are you talking to me?
- Get a nurse over here.

179
00:12:46,198 --> 00:12:48,400
Someone, help!

180
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:53,172
You can do it, Torako!
You can do it, Torako!

181
00:12:53,305 --> 00:12:56,041
Enough! Shut up!

182
00:13:00,312 --> 00:13:02,515
Renal infarction
due to a blood clot.

183
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:07,086
You have renal failure, right?
How long have you been on dialysis?

184
00:13:07,319 --> 00:13:11,357
I won't talk to a surgeon.
Take me to internal medicine.

185
00:13:11,423 --> 00:13:13,559
- This is serious.
- Excuse us.

186
00:13:14,527 --> 00:13:19,298
Executive Manager Mabuchi.
I am terribly sorry.

187
00:13:19,865 --> 00:13:22,334
You were getting dialysis
at a different hospital.

188
00:13:29,909 --> 00:13:33,012
It's renal infarction.
You need to get surgery.

189
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:40,052
I'd rather die
than be operated on by a surgeon.

190
00:13:40,186 --> 00:13:43,289
- You don't care if you die?
- Stop the nonsense.

191
00:13:43,355 --> 00:13:47,326
If heparin doesn't work,
you'll get kidney necrosis and die.

192
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:49,595
Internal medicine can't help.

193
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:57,203
You will be treated
at the surgical department.

194
00:13:59,805 --> 00:14:00,739
Understood?

195
00:14:05,611 --> 00:14:08,080
However, only under one condition.

196
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:12,818
- What is it?
- I'll have Dr. Kondo be in charge.

197
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:20,125
Please take her to a VIP suite
and treat her well.

198
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:21,060
Yes, ma'am.

199
00:14:21,126 --> 00:14:25,497
KAZUYO MABUCHI, EXECUTIVE MANAGER
INTERNAL MEDICINE

200
00:14:29,735 --> 00:14:31,437
- Excuse me.
- What?

201
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:34,306
There are no VIP suites open.

202
00:14:36,342 --> 00:14:40,012
Mrs. Kanie,
you will surely be cured this time.

203
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:45,784
My husband said the surgery dept.
will give their best effort.

204
00:14:46,585 --> 00:14:49,288
- You can do this!
- You can do this!

205
00:14:50,489 --> 00:14:51,423
Yes...

206
00:14:51,857 --> 00:14:55,427
That hurts! Hurry!

207
00:14:58,597 --> 00:15:00,232
Watch where you're going!

208
00:15:00,933 --> 00:15:02,268
That's an expensive painting.

209
00:15:02,334 --> 00:15:05,371
From today, this is also
a VIP suite. Understand?

210
00:15:05,537 --> 00:15:06,472
Yes, sir.

211
00:15:06,705 --> 00:15:08,674
The room isn't important.

212
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:11,143
It is. She is a professor's wife!

213
00:15:11,377 --> 00:15:14,546
Can't she share the VIP suite
with the other wife?

214
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:18,284
That would be absolute hell!

215
00:15:18,350 --> 00:15:20,419
Dr. Daimon, just help us out.

216
00:15:20,486 --> 00:15:23,455
- I won't do that.
- Geez.

217
00:15:25,891 --> 00:15:26,825
Ouch...

218
00:15:27,026 --> 00:15:28,260
It is a big deal.

219
00:15:28,327 --> 00:15:31,297
Human lives are less worthy
than pride?

220
00:15:31,363 --> 00:15:32,431
Pride, of course.

221
00:15:32,631 --> 00:15:35,367
Mrs. Kanie's husband
and Mrs. Mimura's husband

222
00:15:35,467 --> 00:15:37,970
are rivals who joined the hospital
around the same time.

223
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:42,608
Those two wives came from
a powerful family to the hospital,

224
00:15:42,875 --> 00:15:46,578
so they're always
being compared to each other.

225
00:15:47,046 --> 00:15:48,580
Are they family then?

226
00:15:48,714 --> 00:15:51,850
I think they're second cousins.

227
00:15:51,984 --> 00:15:54,853
What's the degree of kinship?

228
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,289
Maybe the sixth degree?

229
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:59,925
Sixth degree, huh...

230
00:16:00,259 --> 00:16:01,126
Ron!

231
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:06,632
Double Ron? You sure are unlucky.

232
00:16:06,699 --> 00:16:09,802
Unbelievable...Help me!

233
00:16:09,935 --> 00:16:12,104
Let me go. I'm going home.

234
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:48,707
I finally found you.

235
00:16:49,208 --> 00:16:53,078
I'll be taking care of Mrs. Mimura
from internal medicine.

236
00:16:54,246 --> 00:16:58,650
After the right kidney is removed,
I'll give her back to them.

237
00:16:58,717 --> 00:17:01,487
- There's a better option.
- What?

238
00:17:02,588 --> 00:17:07,893
Those two are second cousins. Let's
exchange their bowel and kidney.

239
00:17:08,093 --> 00:17:08,927
Exchange?

240
00:17:09,061 --> 00:17:12,231
That's HLA for those wives.

241
00:17:14,666 --> 00:17:16,068
COMPATIBLE

242
00:17:16,468 --> 00:17:17,936
I've never heard.

243
00:17:18,003 --> 00:17:19,938
Of course not. It's never been done.

244
00:17:20,739 --> 00:17:23,876
Living donor transplants
always pose a high risk.

245
00:17:24,076 --> 00:17:26,545
There can be rejection and complication...

246
00:17:26,612 --> 00:17:28,547
But they will both be saved.

247
00:17:30,682 --> 00:17:32,317
That's impossible.

248
00:17:32,451 --> 00:17:35,354
Living donor kidney
and small bowel exchange transplant.

249
00:17:38,424 --> 00:17:39,458
I can do it.

250
00:17:39,591 --> 00:17:41,493
It's not a matter of technique.

251
00:17:42,161 --> 00:17:47,332
This hospital would never let
a marginal surgeon do such an operation.

252
00:17:47,466 --> 00:17:48,834
Who's marginal?

253
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:51,970
- People like you and I.
- Me?

254
00:17:52,104 --> 00:17:58,343
Plus, those two wives are already
on bad terms with each other.

255
00:17:58,410 --> 00:17:59,578
They'd never agree on it.

256
00:17:59,678 --> 00:18:02,981
This is extremely rare.
We should do this.

257
00:18:03,215 --> 00:18:04,049
It's impossible.

258
00:18:07,886 --> 00:18:09,621
What a waste.

259
00:18:27,539 --> 00:18:30,075
Let's begin
this week's preoperative conference.

260
00:18:31,076 --> 00:18:33,712
Torako Mimura, 39,
Prof. Mimura's wife,

261
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:36,248
from the 2nd internal medicine dept.

262
00:18:37,382 --> 00:18:39,151
- Kondo's in charge, right?
- Yes.

263
00:18:40,385 --> 00:18:43,021
Her condition is renal infarction
in the right kidney.

264
00:18:43,388 --> 00:18:45,958
She has renal hypertension.

265
00:18:46,525 --> 00:18:49,428
She has undergone
hemodialysis for two years.

266
00:18:49,728 --> 00:18:52,598
There is no hope
for improvement in both kidneys.

267
00:18:53,198 --> 00:18:55,834
Thus, we'll remove the right kidney.

268
00:18:56,068 --> 00:18:59,872
Why is an instructor
in charge of Prof's wife?

269
00:19:00,038 --> 00:19:01,173
I agree.

270
00:19:01,773 --> 00:19:03,942
Can I move on to the second case?

271
00:19:04,009 --> 00:19:04,843
Please wait.

272
00:19:06,211 --> 00:19:09,681
This is a proposal
for her postoperative care.

273
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,954
Here you are.

274
00:19:19,424 --> 00:19:21,326
Take a look at what I've handed out.

275
00:19:22,528 --> 00:19:24,329
Mrs. Mimura with renal failure and

276
00:19:24,396 --> 00:19:27,599
Mrs. Kanie with bowel failure
are second cousins.

277
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,703
- Their kinship is the sixth degree.
- He stole my idea.

278
00:19:31,904 --> 00:19:36,208
Their blood types are AB
and their HLA's perfectly match.

279
00:19:36,575 --> 00:19:40,345
Both of them meet the requirements
as an organ donor.

280
00:19:40,712 --> 00:19:44,216
This means they can both
be a donor and a recipient

281
00:19:44,816 --> 00:19:47,119
for each other at the same time.

282
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:50,355
What? That's impossible.

283
00:19:50,789 --> 00:19:53,358
Living kidney and small bowel
exchange transplant.

284
00:19:54,326 --> 00:19:55,561
I can do it.

285
00:19:57,963 --> 00:20:00,065
He totally stole this from me.

286
00:20:00,499 --> 00:20:05,070
Sir, we can't let the instructor
do such a risky operation.

287
00:20:05,170 --> 00:20:08,473
The quality of life
for both patients will enhance.

288
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:11,743
But Kondo,

289
00:20:12,945 --> 00:20:18,050
wouldn't you need
two surgeons for this method?

290
00:20:18,116 --> 00:20:19,952
This can't be done by one surgeon.

291
00:20:20,018 --> 00:20:21,486
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

292
00:20:22,454 --> 00:20:26,225
I've already asked
Dr. Daimon to be the other surgeon.

293
00:20:27,593 --> 00:20:32,364
We've already consulted,
and the operative method is perfect.

294
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,299
Are you joking?

295
00:20:34,833 --> 00:20:36,735
Why would you two do this?

296
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:39,738
An instructor and a part-timer.

297
00:20:39,871 --> 00:20:43,809
You all know very well
about Dr. Daimon's technique.

298
00:20:44,643 --> 00:20:49,815
Her small bowel anastomosis skill

299
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:51,617
is the best in this hospital.

300
00:20:53,318 --> 00:20:58,257
I'll have Dr. Daimon be in charge of
Mrs. Kanie's small bowel transplant.

301
00:20:59,491 --> 00:21:01,660
This is absolutely unheard of.

302
00:21:02,527 --> 00:21:04,696
Well, Daimon.

303
00:21:06,798 --> 00:21:09,501
can you do it or not?

304
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:17,776
That's fine. I won't fail.

305
00:21:23,248 --> 00:21:24,149
I see.

306
00:21:25,417 --> 00:21:26,285
Then...

307
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:27,953
I'll allow it.

308
00:21:29,855 --> 00:21:31,923
Sir, I am against this.

309
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:35,694
We risk losing two professors' wives.

310
00:21:36,595 --> 00:21:37,562
Ebina.

311
00:21:39,598 --> 00:21:42,901
I said it's okay.

312
00:21:47,205 --> 00:21:50,242
Yes, sir. I'm sorry.

313
00:21:53,545 --> 00:21:54,646
Thank you very much.

314
00:21:56,114 --> 00:21:57,449
Alright.

315
00:22:05,557 --> 00:22:11,163
Get a surgery consent form
from Professor Kanie's wife.

316
00:22:12,230 --> 00:22:13,165
Yes, sir.

317
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:19,738
You're not going to say
"I'm the doctor in charge," are you?

318
00:22:19,805 --> 00:22:21,807
No. I...

319
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:24,209
Don't worry.

320
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:28,080
You're a candidate
to become the chairperson.

321
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:30,148
Take the easy way.

322
00:22:32,384 --> 00:22:36,755
You shouldn't involve yourself
in a risky operation.

323
00:22:38,223 --> 00:22:39,124
Right?

324
00:22:40,525 --> 00:22:43,028
Don't worry. I'll take care of you.

325
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:45,864
Yes, sir.

326
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,035
The first surgery for this case.

327
00:22:52,738 --> 00:22:57,576
If the surgery succeeds
and it gets published,

328
00:22:57,642 --> 00:22:58,810
it'll surely have an impact.

329
00:23:02,314 --> 00:23:04,983
"Keep your friends close,

330
00:23:05,917 --> 00:23:09,821
and your enemies closer."

331
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:13,425
- Have you ever heard of that?
- No.

332
00:23:13,525 --> 00:23:16,828
It's a classic line
from the movie <i>The Godfather</i>.

333
00:23:19,598 --> 00:23:20,665
I'll be leaving now.

334
00:23:30,675 --> 00:23:33,178
SHINOBU KONDO

335
00:23:36,548 --> 00:23:37,516
Hello?

336
00:23:37,749 --> 00:23:39,384
- You have a phone call.
- From who?

337
00:23:39,851 --> 00:23:41,520
Yamamoto of the Police Department.

338
00:23:43,655 --> 00:23:44,556
Let me talk to him.

339
00:23:45,657 --> 00:23:49,227
Hi, Yamamoto. It's been a while.

340
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:55,867
What may I help the police with?

341
00:23:58,637 --> 00:23:59,504
Right.

342
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:04,443
Michiko Daimon works here.

343
00:24:05,477 --> 00:24:06,344
What?

344
00:24:12,083 --> 00:24:14,553
- Thief.
- Don't praise me.

345
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:18,223
- I don't care since I can operate.
- That's good.

346
00:24:18,757 --> 00:24:23,161
Hold on. Can you do a transplant?

347
00:24:24,729 --> 00:24:29,701
Of course. At least,
as well as any professor here.

348
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:45,851
Here.
It's Mrs. Mimura's consent form.

349
00:24:46,084 --> 00:24:50,055
Thanks. I assure you
the surgery will be a success.

350
00:24:51,289 --> 00:24:56,428
I heard you chose Dr. Daimon
as your partner.

351
00:24:57,863 --> 00:25:02,133
I shouldn't have brought her here
just because of her skill.

352
00:25:03,134 --> 00:25:05,303
Having a wild breed barging in suddenly

353
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:07,906
can have a disrupting effect on the race.

354
00:25:12,611 --> 00:25:15,447
More importantly...

355
00:25:16,414 --> 00:25:17,415
Are you free tonight?

356
00:25:19,618 --> 00:25:23,555
I'm very sorry. I must study
for tomorrow's operation.

357
00:25:25,257 --> 00:25:28,727
Why don't you do it at my place?

358
00:25:30,428 --> 00:25:32,097
I have some really good wine.

359
00:25:36,101 --> 00:25:39,804
Tomorrow's operation is going to
be over ten hours. Good luck.

360
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:42,674
- If you succeed...
- Get paid double.

361
00:25:42,807 --> 00:25:47,379
First, Kondo will take out Mimura's
kidney with renal infarction.

362
00:25:47,512 --> 00:25:52,450
Meanwhile, I take out Kanie's
kidney graft and give it to Kondo.

363
00:25:52,584 --> 00:25:56,721
Next, Kondo removes the small bowel
graft from Mimura.

364
00:25:56,855 --> 00:25:59,858
Then I transplant
the small bowel graft to Kanie.

365
00:25:59,991 --> 00:26:04,229
And then, Kondo transplants
the kidney graft to Mimura,

366
00:26:04,296 --> 00:26:05,397
and it's done.

367
00:26:05,530 --> 00:26:09,968
Finish things up by 5 p.m. I have to
pick up my daughter by then.

368
00:26:10,101 --> 00:26:13,572
Small bowel transplant
takes over ten hours.

369
00:26:14,005 --> 00:26:15,574
I'm fine.

370
00:26:16,975 --> 00:26:20,111
Akira, is Dr. Kondo good?

371
00:26:20,378 --> 00:26:22,080
I don't have much information.

372
00:26:22,414 --> 00:26:25,584
He graduated
from a sub-par university.

373
00:26:25,884 --> 00:26:28,954
How did he get into Teito Hospital?

374
00:26:29,354 --> 00:26:30,689
He may be a dark horse.

375
00:26:32,490 --> 00:26:34,159
Let's go. Final!

376
00:26:38,163 --> 00:26:40,799
Ouch! I got a cramp in my leg.

377
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:10,729
Thanks.

378
00:27:13,965 --> 00:27:17,335
People are talking about it everywhere.

379
00:27:20,105 --> 00:27:23,174
About the operation you're going to do.

380
00:27:23,842 --> 00:27:26,978
Brash for an instructor
to do such a thing?

381
00:27:27,646 --> 00:27:31,650
But if you succeed,
you'll become famous.

382
00:27:32,450 --> 00:27:35,420
You might get closer
to becoming a professor.

383
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:40,025
I'd never even thought of it.

384
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:48,133
Even if you move up the ranks,
don't dump me.

385
00:28:01,813 --> 00:28:04,082
Were you supposed to meet someone?

386
00:28:12,390 --> 00:28:13,358
No way.

387
00:28:23,835 --> 00:28:24,803
Wait here.

388
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:57,869
Mr. Kondo?

389
00:28:58,203 --> 00:29:00,438
I forgot to give you the files.

390
00:29:04,876 --> 00:29:09,581
Small bowel will take more time,
so I'll give it to you by noon.

391
00:29:09,714 --> 00:29:11,182
Don't worry about me.

392
00:29:11,316 --> 00:29:14,753
It's an honor to be able to
do an operation with you.

393
00:29:15,453 --> 00:29:17,088
Thanks for working with me.

394
00:29:20,625 --> 00:29:23,528
We now begin Mrs. Mimura's
right kidney removal,

395
00:29:23,828 --> 00:29:27,699
and living donor kidney
and small bowel exchange transplant.

396
00:29:28,333 --> 00:29:31,369
- Are you ready?
- Yes, sir.

397
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:35,306
First, remove the right kidney
with renal infarction.

398
00:29:36,541 --> 00:29:40,178
Blood pressure is 90/55.
Pulse is 80 and sinus.

399
00:29:40,945 --> 00:29:42,447
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

400
00:29:44,549 --> 00:29:49,354
We now begin Mrs. Kanie's left kidney
removal and small bowel transplant...

401
00:29:53,758 --> 00:29:55,293
Are we ready?

402
00:29:56,327 --> 00:29:57,729
- Mosquito pean.
- Here.

403
00:30:00,598 --> 00:30:03,935
That subordinate of yours
is pretty skilled.

404
00:30:04,402 --> 00:30:06,371
Thank you very much.

405
00:30:06,771 --> 00:30:09,407
It will be big news if it succeeds.

406
00:30:09,874 --> 00:30:13,011
Living donor kidney
and small bowel exchange transplant.

407
00:30:13,077 --> 00:30:17,081
It'll be called
the "Kondo Operative Method."

408
00:30:21,719 --> 00:30:22,887
- Metzen.
- Yes.

409
00:30:29,627 --> 00:30:32,664
The kidney graft has been removed.
Take it.

410
00:30:33,731 --> 00:30:34,566
That's fast!

411
00:30:43,775 --> 00:30:47,979
Stop the bleeding
and perform intraperitoneal lavage.

412
00:30:48,146 --> 00:30:49,814
Get me 2,000cc of warm saline.

413
00:30:50,415 --> 00:30:51,583
Monopolar.

414
00:30:51,716 --> 00:30:53,151
Renal vein resection is done.

415
00:30:53,284 --> 00:30:56,321
Now detach the renal fascia
and the tissue.

416
00:30:56,988 --> 00:30:57,822
- Kelly.
- Here.

417
00:31:02,026 --> 00:31:02,961
Here you are.

418
00:31:03,428 --> 00:31:06,798
Dr. Daimon has removed the kidney graft.

419
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:09,734
Already? It's only been an hour.

420
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:16,007
Blood pressure has dropped to 60.

421
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:18,109
- Suction, please.
- Yes.

422
00:31:18,543 --> 00:31:19,978
- Suction over here too.
- Yes.

423
00:31:21,412 --> 00:31:22,881
Is everything OK?

424
00:31:24,082 --> 00:31:26,050
What's wrong? Arterial trauma?

425
00:31:26,117 --> 00:31:27,252
Performing pressure hemostasis.

426
00:31:27,986 --> 00:31:28,853
Gauze.

427
00:31:37,595 --> 00:31:41,366
He's late. Go take a look next door.

428
00:31:41,432 --> 00:31:45,436
He's not late. You're just too fast.

429
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:48,740
This is operating room No.3.

430
00:31:50,074 --> 00:31:52,777
Dr. Daimon, it's from Dr. Jonouchi.

431
00:31:57,048 --> 00:31:57,916
Is something wrong?

432
00:31:58,683 --> 00:31:59,651
- Gauze.
- Yes.

433
00:31:59,784 --> 00:32:01,286
He can't stop the patient bleeding.

434
00:32:01,953 --> 00:32:04,822
It's been like this
for an hour now.

435
00:32:05,056 --> 00:32:06,658
What are we going to do?

436
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:10,061
At this rate,
we'll lose two wives of professors.

437
00:32:10,528 --> 00:32:13,097
- This is bad!
- I'll take over.

438
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:22,807
Let me help you.

439
00:32:30,515 --> 00:32:31,349
Dr. Daimon.

440
00:32:31,616 --> 00:32:34,118
Apply pressure along the kidney.
Increase suction too.

441
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:37,221
Kondo, separate the retroperitoneum.

442
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:39,891
- Yes. Mayo scissors.
- Put my loupe down.

443
00:32:40,558 --> 00:32:41,559
Excuse me.

444
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:43,127
Check the inferior vena cava.

445
00:32:45,463 --> 00:32:48,533
Right there! A laceration
in the inferior vena cava.

446
00:32:50,234 --> 00:32:52,370
- Move. I'll do it.
- Kelly.

447
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:56,174
I make continuous sutures with 5-0.

448
00:33:00,778 --> 00:33:01,813
- Metzen.
- Yes.

449
00:33:07,385 --> 00:33:09,821
Blood pressure is 95/60.
Pulse rate is 80.

450
00:33:10,922 --> 00:33:13,992
Bleeding point is complete.
Now separate the urinary duct.

451
00:33:14,292 --> 00:33:15,259
Narrow-tipped kelly.

452
00:33:17,228 --> 00:33:19,564
I thought my heart would stop.

453
00:33:21,966 --> 00:33:25,169
The right kidney is removed.
Next, the small bowel graft.

454
00:33:25,436 --> 00:33:27,138
A very small amount of urine.

455
00:33:27,638 --> 00:33:31,142
I'll do the kidney transplant first.
Move.

456
00:33:31,476 --> 00:33:34,846
- But...
- I'm fast. Metzen.

457
00:33:35,913 --> 00:33:37,515
- Metzen!
- Yes.

458
00:33:40,818 --> 00:33:42,286
- Metzen!
- Yes.

459
00:33:52,897 --> 00:33:54,365
Operating room No.1.

460
00:33:54,932 --> 00:33:56,968
It's from operating room No.3.

461
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:58,036
Ask them what they want.

462
00:33:59,303 --> 00:34:02,673
There are frequent PVCs.
Tell her to return.

463
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:06,110
Use lidocaine
so I'll have another hour.

464
00:34:06,611 --> 00:34:08,279
You sure make people work hard.

465
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:11,582
- Any longer than an hour is bad.
- Alright.

466
00:34:14,685 --> 00:34:17,121
An hour? That's ridiculous.

467
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:18,356
Mosquito.

468
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:33,037
The small bowel graft is removed.

469
00:34:33,337 --> 00:34:35,506
- No way.
- I go get the small bowel.

470
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:39,110
Dr. Kondo,
take care of the rest, please.

471
00:34:39,844 --> 00:34:41,079
Yes.

472
00:34:49,053 --> 00:34:50,088
How much time has passed?

473
00:34:50,221 --> 00:34:55,560
Both the transplant and
the removal took exactly an hour.

474
00:34:56,694 --> 00:35:00,531
She ended up doing everything by herself.

475
00:35:02,266 --> 00:35:07,438
So does that mean that
the part-timer is the best one here?

476
00:35:09,907 --> 00:35:10,942
I'm sorry.

477
00:35:16,747 --> 00:35:19,183
You're late. It's been
1 hour and 2 minutes.

478
00:35:19,517 --> 00:35:21,786
Blood pressure is 119/80. Sinus.

479
00:35:22,053 --> 00:35:23,821
- She's stable.
- How did it go?

480
00:35:24,055 --> 00:35:26,991
- They're sewing her up.
- You're done already?

481
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:31,062
Combine the small bowel graft
and the mesenteric artery.

482
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:31,996
Use 7-0 nylon.

483
00:36:02,193 --> 00:36:03,294
Dr. Kondo.

484
00:36:04,829 --> 00:36:06,364
Nice work.

485
00:36:37,495 --> 00:36:43,467
- I still can't eat? Hurry up.
- Quiet!

486
00:36:43,534 --> 00:36:45,269
We start with the tongue.

487
00:36:45,336 --> 00:36:49,106
- Who cares what we start with?
- Grill it, okay?

488
00:36:49,173 --> 00:36:52,076
- You're like a kid.
- This is tongue?

489
00:36:55,346 --> 00:36:58,282
- You are so full of energy.
- I'm back.

490
00:36:58,549 --> 00:36:59,550
Hi.

491
00:36:59,617 --> 00:37:01,786
That looks delicious.

492
00:37:01,953 --> 00:37:06,290
- Thanks for picking her up.
- There was big trouble.

493
00:37:06,357 --> 00:37:11,128
Two classes had a fight
over the sandbox.

494
00:37:11,295 --> 00:37:15,433
- Really?
- Akira made us be friends again.

495
00:37:15,566 --> 00:37:19,637
They got quiet when I gave these.
Kids are easy to please.

496
00:37:19,770 --> 00:37:22,940
You even do things
behind the scenes with kids.

497
00:37:23,140 --> 00:37:24,742
So how did it go today?

498
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:30,147
Great!

499
00:37:30,781 --> 00:37:33,484
- Of course.
- I'll deliver the bill.

500
00:37:33,818 --> 00:37:37,021
Hey Daimon,
do I get paid double too?

501
00:37:38,456 --> 00:37:39,924
I don't know.

502
00:37:41,759 --> 00:37:45,563
- Akira, how does that work?
- I told you.

503
00:37:45,630 --> 00:37:48,132
I didn't hear about this.

504
00:37:48,466 --> 00:37:49,900
I told you...

505
00:37:52,436 --> 00:37:54,005
That's my meat!

506
00:37:56,507 --> 00:37:59,443
I am so happy for you.

507
00:37:59,577 --> 00:38:01,445
Thank you so much.

508
00:38:02,380 --> 00:38:06,550
You have wonderful doctors, Dr. Ebina.

509
00:38:06,784 --> 00:38:08,152
Oh, yes...

510
00:38:08,419 --> 00:38:11,289
You're doing well, but please rest well.

511
00:38:14,825 --> 00:38:16,861
I feel so embarrassed now,

512
00:38:17,728 --> 00:38:20,798
making a fuss over
internal medicine and surgery.

513
00:38:21,499 --> 00:38:25,503
That's why we're going to
leave the Shirobara Club.

514
00:38:26,370 --> 00:38:30,241
We promised
we won't care about departments.

515
00:38:30,574 --> 00:38:34,011
We'll get together
to work for Teito Hospital.

516
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,547
Since we received the transplant,

517
00:38:36,614 --> 00:38:40,451
we'll mediate between
these two departments, hopefully.

518
00:38:40,985 --> 00:38:43,287
I am so glad to hear that.

519
00:38:43,854 --> 00:38:48,359
The territorial dispute of
the motorcycle gangs is over, huh.

520
00:38:48,926 --> 00:38:49,827
Quiet!

521
00:38:54,899 --> 00:38:57,435
Will you proofread this for me?

522
00:38:57,635 --> 00:38:59,070
Oh, it's done.

523
00:39:00,237 --> 00:39:04,041
Living donor kidney and small bowel
exchange transplant surgery.

524
00:39:05,209 --> 00:39:07,178
This is wonderful.

525
00:39:08,279 --> 00:39:10,448
This is the very first case.

526
00:39:11,382 --> 00:39:16,454
This is a great achievement for
our hospital, no, the medical society.

527
00:39:18,456 --> 00:39:19,590
Speaking honestly,

528
00:39:19,790 --> 00:39:24,295
I did not think
you were this capable.

529
00:39:25,129 --> 00:39:26,163
Thank you, sir.

530
00:39:26,831 --> 00:39:29,967
May I publicize this
at the next academic conference?

531
00:39:30,234 --> 00:39:32,002
Of course.

532
00:39:33,437 --> 00:39:37,241
But I wonder what would've happened

533
00:39:37,308 --> 00:39:41,145
if Daimon wasn't present
for this operation.

534
00:39:43,581 --> 00:39:46,951
I don't know.
She was included in my plan.

535
00:39:53,023 --> 00:39:58,896
I had underestimated you.

536
00:40:00,498 --> 00:40:04,869
I see how you are. Wow. Okay.

537
00:40:07,972 --> 00:40:10,007
Do you play golf?

538
00:40:10,541 --> 00:40:12,209
Yes, but I'm not good.

539
00:40:12,276 --> 00:40:14,712
It's fine as long as you can hit the ball.

540
00:40:16,180 --> 00:40:19,583
Can you keep your schedule open
this weekend?

541
00:40:20,951 --> 00:40:25,089
I think I'd want you to meet my daughter.

542
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:27,591
Thank you very much.

543
00:40:28,692 --> 00:40:31,362
I'll make sure things go well for you.

544
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:33,431
Excuse me, sir.

545
00:40:41,972 --> 00:40:45,843
Thank you for
working with Daimon and Jonouchi.

546
00:40:47,011 --> 00:40:47,845
Please.

547
00:40:48,779 --> 00:40:52,216
Professor.
Here's a melon. Here's a bill.

548
00:41:00,925 --> 00:41:06,263
That horse of yours runs very well
and is quite a nice horse.

549
00:41:06,764 --> 00:41:07,798
Excuse my word,

550
00:41:08,065 --> 00:41:11,569
but she has much experience,
unlike Dr. Kondo.

551
00:41:11,635 --> 00:41:12,736
That's fine.

552
00:41:14,438 --> 00:41:16,607
He's fine like that.

553
00:41:17,007 --> 00:41:21,779
Skills in surgery don't matter
for becoming a professor.

554
00:41:22,079 --> 00:41:25,216
Is Dr. Kondo going to become a professor?

555
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:29,019
They bravely perform operations

556
00:41:29,620 --> 00:41:33,390
that don't have an established method
and have low success rates.

557
00:41:34,725 --> 00:41:36,961
They put patients' lives on the line.

558
00:41:37,628 --> 00:41:41,131
They brag and call themselves Doctor-X.

559
00:41:43,100 --> 00:41:44,201
A group...

560
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:49,840
that challenges dangerous craft.

561
00:41:51,108 --> 00:41:52,877
What are you talking about?

562
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:55,880
Is Daimon one of them?

563
00:41:59,116 --> 00:42:02,253
Public Security Bureau
of the Police Dept. called me.

564
00:42:02,620 --> 00:42:03,687
Public Security Bureau?

565
00:42:04,321 --> 00:42:07,091
At the Davydenko Memorial Hospital
in Russia,

566
00:42:07,992 --> 00:42:09,159
there was a female doctor

567
00:42:10,127 --> 00:42:14,932
who performed unauthorized
living donor lung transplant.

568
00:42:16,767 --> 00:42:18,602
What are you talking about?

569
00:42:19,236 --> 00:42:20,571
I'll ask you once again.

570
00:42:21,505 --> 00:42:24,542
Is that female doctor...Daimon?

571
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:27,077
I have no idea.

572
00:42:38,489 --> 00:42:43,527
Oh my! Three million yen is expensive.

573
00:42:43,827 --> 00:42:48,098
It's the first case ever, and it comes
along with a thesis and secrecy.

574
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:51,835
- It's very reasonable.
- You're right.

575
00:42:54,805 --> 00:42:56,840
It certainly is reasonable.

576
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:03,914
Three million yen...

577
00:43:06,417 --> 00:43:08,786
20TH ANNIVERSARY OF THE SHIROBARA CLUB

578
00:43:10,054 --> 00:43:12,056
Have you seen Torako?

579
00:43:12,523 --> 00:43:14,258
- No.
- I see.

580
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:18,062
Do you know where Torako is?

581
00:43:19,430 --> 00:43:20,764
I see.

582
00:43:23,334 --> 00:43:27,304
Excuse me. Do you know where
Mrs. Kanie and Mrs. Mimura are?

583
00:43:27,671 --> 00:43:31,008
I've never heard of those people.

584
00:43:49,827 --> 00:43:52,463
They were both demoted?

585
00:43:53,797 --> 00:43:58,068
Of course. That's how
the university hospital goes.

586
00:43:59,436 --> 00:44:00,337
Okay.

587
00:44:01,271 --> 00:44:03,007
You're doing really well.

588
00:44:04,708 --> 00:44:06,877
I'm so proud of you.

589
00:44:06,944 --> 00:44:08,712
I owe it all to you.

590
00:44:09,813 --> 00:44:15,519
Are you ready for the convention
in Paris next week?

591
00:44:16,220 --> 00:44:19,056
Actually, I won't be able to
join you this time.

592
00:44:20,624 --> 00:44:21,925
What do you mean?

593
00:44:23,360 --> 00:44:25,529
Prof. Hiruma asked me
to help with his thesis.

594
00:44:27,097 --> 00:44:28,132
I see.

595
00:44:41,845 --> 00:44:43,347
Yesterday's surgery was amazing.

596
00:44:43,947 --> 00:44:47,351
You came up with
the exchange transplant, right?

597
00:44:47,918 --> 00:44:50,788
That's so amazing.
When did you come up with it?

598
00:44:57,327 --> 00:44:58,328
Dr. Daimon.

599
00:45:00,664 --> 00:45:02,800
Thank you so much.

600
00:45:08,439 --> 00:45:09,807
I won't do that.

601
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:14,578
That's so rude. You did
the operation, thanks to Dr. Kondo.

602
00:45:14,645 --> 00:45:15,612
That's okay.

603
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:18,916
I look forward to
working with you again.

604
00:45:22,786 --> 00:45:26,123
I won't help you get promoted.

605
00:45:26,190 --> 00:45:28,659
<i>She hates groups and being controlled.</i>

606
00:45:29,193 --> 00:45:33,497
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

607
00:45:33,897 --> 00:45:35,833
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

608
00:45:35,899 --> 00:45:38,936
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

609
00:46:48,839 --> 00:46:50,941
THE STORY DEPICTED IN THIS DRAMA
IS FICTITIOUS

610
00:46:51,074 --> 00:46:52,309
You'll die if I don't operate.

611
00:46:52,442 --> 00:46:55,078
I won't leave my life to a part-timer.

612
00:46:55,212 --> 00:46:56,747
Don't let Daimon near her.

613
00:46:56,880 --> 00:46:58,882
I will expose all your secrets.

614
00:46:59,016 --> 00:47:01,351
Please operate on me.

615
00:47:01,485 --> 00:47:04,188
You're going to betray me?

616
00:47:04,254 --> 00:47:05,889
Cardiac arrest.
